// @hash 20c51d6bc82e
// @legend — how to write this file (rewritten by ./singularity build; edits inside this block are lost):
//   Item: "<key>" (terse; <key> is "<pluginId>:<id>")
//   Hide: { "item": "<key>", "hidden": true }
//   Spacer (gap): { "type": "spacer", "id": "<unique-id>" } — grows to push every item after it to the far end of the row (title left, chips right); at most one per slot. Use it instead of a second slot.
//   Group: { "type": "header", "label": "<title>", "collapsed": false, "items": [ "<key>", … ] }
//   Overflow (⋯ menu): { "type": "overflow", "id": "<unique-id>", "items": [ "<key>", … ] }
// The backup run-detail pane, top to bottom.
//
// Archive first: it is one line — how big the archive came out — and it is the
// first question asked of a finished backup, because nothing else on the row
// answers it. A nightly archive that quietly halves is a source that stopped
// contributing, and `outcome` cannot report that.
//
// Sources before Targets because that is the order the run happened in: a
// backup gathers what goes into the archive, then dispatches the archive to
// each storage target. It is also the order the hand-rolled card this pane
// replaced used.
//
// Targets is last but not lesser — it is the one that opens itself when a
// target failed (`useDefaultOpen`), because it holds the Grant access button,
// the only in-app repair path for a storage target whose OAuth token expired.
{
  "items": [
    "backup.runs-arm:archive",
    "backup.runs-arm:sources",
    "backup.runs-arm:targets"
  ]
}
